#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087511 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e4bb90c5-2794-5657-8f0b-45eb64873e03" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Cubic Polynomial Given One Real Root, Two Complex Roots, and a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/id #uuid "c7cc2dca-cc41-561c-bc48-bbcda272dd71" :question/math-academy-id "e-5792" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/assets/1c498dcdef2a71cc27117c2c0a43dd54074128ec3e5693e13a12d18b660d1cf4.png)\n\nThe Argand diagram above shows the roots of the cubic polynomial $f(x).$ Find $f(x)$ given that the coefficient of the cubic term is $1.$" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we see that $f(x)$ has roots ${\\color{black}x_1= 2}$ and ${\\color{black}x_{2,3}=-2\\pm \\textrm{i}}.$ Additionally, we're given that the coefficient of the cubic term is ${\\color{black}a=1}.$ \n\nTherefore, we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =(x-2)(x-(-2+\\text{i}))(x-(-2-\\text{i}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-2)(x-(-2+\\text{i}))(x-(-2-\\text{i})) & = \\\\ (x-2)({x}^{2}-x(-2-\\text{i})-x(-2+\\text{i})+(-2+\\text{i})(-2-\\text{i})) & = \\\\ (x-2)({x}^{2}+4x+5) & = \\\\ {x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+5x-2{x}^{2}-8x-10 & = \\\\ {x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}-3x-10 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x) = x^3+2x^2-3x-10.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087586 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "517f2054-008e-54eb-89dd-5f0a09e1f881" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Cubic Polynomial Given Three Real Roots and a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/id #uuid "92ac2f4f-d0a5-5ccb-9213-87495927ccb8" :question/math-academy-id "e-8799" :question/problem "The cubic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots $x_1=x_2=2,x_3=1,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $3.$ Find $P(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Since our cubic polynomial has roots ${\\color{black}x_1=x_2=2}$ and ${\\color{black}x_3=1},$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is ${\\color{black}a=3},$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) & =3(x-2)(x-2)(x-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(x-2)(x-2)(x-1) & =3({x}^{2}-4x+4)(x-1) \\\\  & =3({x}^{3}-{x}^{2}-4{x}^{2}+4x+4x-4) \\\\  & =3({x}^{3}-5{x}^{2}+8x-4) \\\\  & =3{x}^{3}-15{x}^{2}+24x-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x) = 3x^3 -15x^2+24x-12.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087906 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "517f2054-008e-54eb-89dd-5f0a09e1f881" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Cubic Polynomial Given Three Real Roots and a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8db889c3-c19c-5637-8aef-e1488900d7f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x^{3} + 3x^{2} - 5x - 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084448} {:answer/id #uuid "9b775426-0b4f-5aee-a02d-2ee9686862ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x^{3} - 6x^{2} - 2x + 6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084449} {:answer/id #uuid "e449695a-8f8f-5e9f-a2a6-24133c819e3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x^{3} + 6x^{2} - 10x - 6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084450} {:answer/id #uuid "4cd8afc3-e54c-54fa-9a89-624662056e76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x^{3} - x^{2} - 5x - 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084451} {:answer/id #uuid "6688e61b-1b6d-5272-ac24-4f9f18d22e29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x^{3} - 2x^{2} - 10x - 6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084452}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6688e61b-1b6d-5272-ac24-4f9f18d22e29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x^{3} - 2x^{2} - 10x - 6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084452} :answer-field/id #uuid "d7715e05-200b-56ba-8e5a-acabfe7ef760" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084447}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2ce33460-dd2f-51a5-8e90-45e056aed429" :question/math-academy-id "q-101622" :question/problem "The cubic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=-1,{x}_{3}=3,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $2.$ Find $P(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Since our cubic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=-1$ and ${x}_{3}=3,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=2,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) & =2(x-(-1))(x-(-1))(x-3) \\\\  & =2(x+1)(x+1)(x-3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(x+1)(x+1)(x-3) & =2({x}^{2}+2x+1)(x-3) \\\\  & =2({x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}+2{x}^{2}-6x+x-3) \\\\  & =2({x}^{3}-{x}^{2}-5x-3) \\\\  & =2{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-10x-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=2{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-10x-6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087915 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "517f2054-008e-54eb-89dd-5f0a09e1f881" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Cubic Polynomial Given Three Real Roots and a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae36425f-5e48-5d4f-8932-3a137c1f94e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x^{3} - 8x^{2} + 10x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084502} {:answer/id #uuid "e7f7b873-fb65-5a93-bedf-1b8d8b3b6cd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x^{3} + 4x^{2} + 10x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084503} {:answer/id #uuid "154b65e5-ff43-514f-b226-ec2977e6cc3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x^{3} - 4x^{2} - 10x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084504} {:answer/id #uuid "20ed9f7e-6cd2-5097-861e-c62eb98176d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x^{3} + 8x^{2} + 5x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084505} {:answer/id #uuid "291c4f7d-5ed3-53a3-8a1a-28b5bab60d35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x^{3} + 4x^{2} - 5x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084506}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ae36425f-5e48-5d4f-8932-3a137c1f94e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x^{3} - 8x^{2} + 10x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084502} :answer-field/id #uuid "159db6ae-8ceb-5e94-ae54-fd52d97b24a6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084501}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9b7607d8-f365-578e-840c-7619cca90194" :question/math-academy-id "q-104469" :question/problem "The cubic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=-5,$ ${x}_{2}=0,$ and ${x}_{3}=1,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $-2.$ Find $P(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Since our cubic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}=-5,$ ${x}_{1}=0,$ and ${x}_{3}=1,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=-2,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) & =-2(x-(-5))(x-0)(x-1) \\\\  & =-2x(x+5)(x-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x(x+5)(x-1) & =-2x({x}^{2}+4x-5) \\\\  & =-2({x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-5x) \\\\  & =-2{x}^{3}-8{x}^{2}+10x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=-2{x}^{3}-8{x}^{2}+10x.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278507 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "517f2054-008e-54eb-89dd-5f0a09e1f881" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Cubic Polynomial Given Three Real Roots and a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0754b73c-fa0c-567e-acd4-6eaaf32f9cb6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{x}^{3}-25{x}^{2}-15x+45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278509} {:answer/id #uuid "e64b1bc0-4d6b-54e8-b11c-deb9fa0001fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{x}^{3}+5{x}^{2}+5x-25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278510} {:answer/id #uuid "11e24a1f-9de8-5ca7-8645-f700caaedb6e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{x}^{3}+15{x}^{2}+25x-45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278511} {:answer/id #uuid "b9629441-8cc3-5391-a858-baf3a9959af0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{x}^{3}+25{x}^{2}+15x-45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278512} {:answer/id #uuid "1fe85ecf-145d-5018-b8fa-5445a7fc278d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{x}^{3}+15{x}^{2}+5x-25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278513}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b9629441-8cc3-5391-a858-baf3a9959af0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{x}^{3}+25{x}^{2}+15x-45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278512} :answer-field/id #uuid "7333ba0b-5812-5133-89d3-8ceabb4b2716" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278508}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "96760cb6-c1a1-5102-a49a-28f41c5afd39" :question/math-academy-id "q-104471" :question/problem "The cubic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=-3,{x}_{3}=1,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $5.$ Find $P(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Since our cubic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=-3$ and ${x}_{3}=1,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=5,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) & =5(x-(-3))(x-(-3))(x-1) \\\\  & =5(x+3)(x+3)(x-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(x+3)(x+3)(x-1) & =5({x}^{2}+6x+9)(x-1) \\\\  & =5({x}^{3}-{x}^{2}+6{x}^{2}-6x+9x-9) \\\\  & =5({x}^{3}+5{x}^{2}+3x-9) \\\\  & =5{x}^{3}+25{x}^{2}+15x-45.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=5{x}^{3}+25{x}^{2}+15x-45.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278514 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e4bb90c5-2794-5657-8f0b-45eb64873e03" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Cubic Polynomial Given One Real Root, Two Complex Roots, and a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b5a45ed8-2813-5d60-9ff3-b09265015e45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+4x-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278516} {:answer/id #uuid "43d6ed9e-848a-5fd1-bcb4-6ae1b774f1ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+2x-20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278517} {:answer/id #uuid "7d0741fd-6970-52b4-95a4-fb9bbe6b628d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+2x+20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278518} {:answer/id #uuid "3f498c06-f756-52f6-82c1-22e7aca54793" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}-2x+20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278519} {:answer/id #uuid "4966277c-50e9-5723-909a-f77ecee246e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}-4x+10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278520}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "43d6ed9e-848a-5fd1-bcb4-6ae1b774f1ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+2x-20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278517} :answer-field/id #uuid "80fba6b1-2db0-5303-820f-da06609dd2b9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278515}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "91e3d52c-5018-52b0-b9ab-ad5d3cbe5223" :question/math-academy-id "q-104489" :question/problem "The cubic polynomial $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=-2,{x}_{2,3}=3\\pm \\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $-1.$ Find $f(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Since $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=-2$ and ${x}_{2,3}=3\\pm \\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=-1,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =-1(x-(-2))(x-(3+\\text{i}))(x-(3-\\text{i})) \\\\  & =-(x+2)(x-(3+\\text{i}))(x-(3-\\text{i}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-(x+2)(x-(3+\\text{i}))(x-(3-\\text{i})) & = \\\\ -(x+2)({x}^{2}-x(3-\\text{i})-x(3+\\text{i})+(3+\\text{i})(3-\\text{i})) & = \\\\ -(x+2)({x}^{2}-6x+10) & = \\\\ -({x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}+10x+2{x}^{2}-12x+20) & = \\\\ -{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+2x-20 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=-{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+2x-20.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278521 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "517f2054-008e-54eb-89dd-5f0a09e1f881" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Cubic Polynomial Given Three Real Roots and a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a9aa6391-e74c-5e7d-b32f-4bbc6369d2a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278523} {:answer/id #uuid "03523142-f6c3-5749-8915-f4be6e63e2c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+15x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278524} {:answer/id #uuid "a0f4cf92-b55b-5d11-9655-297a72d2ca0a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{3}+8{x}^{2}+60x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278525} {:answer/id #uuid "4e54367d-c5be-5cbc-a12f-185464386bb5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{3}-4x-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278526} {:answer/id #uuid "94b67589-28b7-58bd-989a-b361536a8da2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}-30x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278527}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "94b67589-28b7-58bd-989a-b361536a8da2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}-30x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278527} :answer-field/id #uuid "f004ce36-6d59-501f-b5c1-eaf5720e928d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278522}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e37f8325-e464-5e55-be70-5b16127326eb" :question/math-academy-id "q-107540" :question/problem "The cubic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=-3,$ ${x}_{2}=0,$ and ${x}_{3}=5,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $2.$ Find $P(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Since our cubic equation has roots ${x}_{1}=-3,$ ${x}_{2}=0,$ and ${x}_{3}=5,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=2,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) & =2(x-(-3))(x-0)(x-5) \\\\  & =2x(x+3)(x-5)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x(x+3)(x-5) & =2x({x}^{2}-2x-15) \\\\  & =2({x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-15x) \\\\  & =2{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}-30x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=2{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}-30x.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278528 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e4bb90c5-2794-5657-8f0b-45eb64873e03" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Cubic Polynomial Given One Real Root, Two Complex Roots, and a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3abb6aa4-e557-5e95-bfb5-0a6523993a2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}-{x}^{2}+16x-16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278530} {:answer/id #uuid "b9a9a5b1-efcf-5fcc-a86f-7e5bc83cc6b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}+16x+16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278531} {:answer/id #uuid "4de6c775-96bb-5d4b-83dd-c4c76dc02a6d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}+32x+32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278532} {:answer/id #uuid "e9685cdd-d84f-5498-8601-1fa2914d71a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}+16x+32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278533} {:answer/id #uuid "6ba8dd3d-6f6b-546e-86bc-ac69fd19628d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+32x-32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278534}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4de6c775-96bb-5d4b-83dd-c4c76dc02a6d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}+32x+32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278532} :answer-field/id #uuid "7024d7e6-599e-5348-8599-2341fcd3bba7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278529}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "35e8d73b-cad1-5357-8f7d-d049b5fbd1f8" :question/math-academy-id "q-107541" :question/problem "The cubic polynomial $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=-1,{x}_{2,3}=\\pm 4\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $2.$ Find $f(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Since $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=-1$ and ${x}_{2,3}=\\pm 4\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=2,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =2(x-(-1))(x-4\\text{i})(x-(-4\\text{i})) \\\\  & =2(x+1)(x-4\\text{i})(x+4\\text{i})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(x+1)(x-4\\text{i})(x+4\\text{i}) & = \\\\ 2(x+1)({x}^{2}-(4\\text{i})^{2}) & = \\\\ 2(x+1)({x}^{2}+16) & = \\\\ 2({x}^{3}+{x}^{2}+16x+16) & = \\\\ 2{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}+32x+32 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=2{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}+32x+32.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278535 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e4bb90c5-2794-5657-8f0b-45eb64873e03" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Cubic Polynomial Given One Real Root, Two Complex Roots, and a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27a51973-2aaf-59d1-bfad-18627b7ab64f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}+9x-36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278537} {:answer/id #uuid "7d6e2840-e270-59a4-8d60-c00f23f258ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}-8{x}^{2}+10x-14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278538} {:answer/id #uuid "56171563-0615-5fb3-b854-9300e0b02d03" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278539} {:answer/id #uuid "ef6e91be-e836-5466-8026-ab7735b0b298" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+3x-18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278540} {:answer/id #uuid "a4bd8db2-376d-5ea8-89f5-d2d2a68965c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}-5{x}^{2}+16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278541}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "27a51973-2aaf-59d1-bfad-18627b7ab64f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}+9x-36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278537} :answer-field/id #uuid "9da7061c-555a-54eb-aa9f-d21b81deaa88" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278536}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "54688a98-1474-5993-a7d9-b3966da03d6d" :question/math-academy-id "q-17407" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/assets/b771ac7e3d7e724b1eae9ebfc592d36a903a1fc46cc2aac5a55ea9517dc2ce12.png)\n\nThe Argand diagram above shows the roots of a cubic polynomial $f(x).$\nFind $f(x)$ given that the coefficient of the cubic term is $1.$" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we see that $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=4$ and ${x}_{2,3}=\\pm 3\\text{i}.$ Additionally, we're given that the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=1.$ Therefore, we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =1(x-4)(x-3\\text{i})(x-(-3\\text{i})) \\\\  & =(x-4)(x-3\\text{i})(x+3\\text{i})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-4)(x-3\\text{i})(x+3\\text{i}) & = \\\\ (x-4)({x}^{2}-x(-3\\text{i})-x(3\\text{i})+(3\\text{i})(-3\\text{i})) & = \\\\ (x-4)({x}^{2}+9) & = \\\\ {x}^{3}+9x-4{x}^{2}-36 & = \\\\ {x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}+9x-36 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)={x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}+9x-36.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278542 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e4bb90c5-2794-5657-8f0b-45eb64873e03" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Cubic Polynomial Given One Real Root, Two Complex Roots, and a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30d61b72-be3b-5b60-81da-c6004c3d8bb7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278544} {:answer/id #uuid "027dc068-9737-5fc9-940e-9cbcd0ca6fdd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278545}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "027dc068-9737-5fc9-940e-9cbcd0ca6fdd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278545} :answer-field/id #uuid "5453f529-0725-5102-b8c9-1ce607abae81" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278543} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a78ceb2-9cc6-5d93-887b-25eb96b9ca89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278547}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1a78ceb2-9cc6-5d93-887b-25eb96b9ca89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278547} :answer-field/id #uuid "18022453-d070-5b0c-9910-f2940240d6c4" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278546} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "75a7947f-a458-5b9b-b4c6-8619b89af7cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "95" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278549}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "75a7947f-a458-5b9b-b4c6-8619b89af7cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "95" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278549} :answer-field/id #uuid "fa5ca1e3-e270-5d63-8c7f-a4fface8a7c4" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278548} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "df2c67de-7b80-500f-a702-aaae9e6c8136" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "65" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278551}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "df2c67de-7b80-500f-a702-aaae9e6c8136" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "65" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278551} :answer-field/id #uuid "ea785752-b49f-58e4-8622-574073534e7d" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278550}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "96a0a3e4-159f-50b4-bed9-d153893e944f" :question/math-academy-id "q-275172" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/assets/210d2120771bef60b0db703a04a06df395225a0c9a884faf012d55f0ed1f60d6.png)\n\nThe Argand diagram above shows the roots of the cubic polynomial $f(x).$ Find $f(x)$ given that the coefficient of the cubic term is $5.$\n\n$f(x)=$\n{{field-1}}${x}^{3}\\,-$\n{{field-2}}${x}^{2}\\,+$\n{{field-3}}$x\\,-$\n{{field-4}}" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we see that $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=1$ and ${x}_{2,3}=3\\pm 2\\text{i}.$ Additionally, we're given that the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=5.$ Therefore, we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =5(x-1)(x-(3+2\\text{i}))(x-(3-2\\text{i}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(x-1)(x-(3+2\\text{i}))(x-(3-2\\text{i})) & = \\\\ 5(x-1)({x}^{2}-x(3-2\\text{i})-x(3+2\\text{i})+(3+2\\text{i})(3-2\\text{i})) & = \\\\ 5(x-1)({x}^{2}-6x+13) & = \\\\ 5({x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}+13x-{x}^{2}+6x-13) & = \\\\ 5{x}^{3}-35{x}^{2}+95x-65.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=5{x}^{3}-35{x}^{2}+95x-65.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278552 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "517f2054-008e-54eb-89dd-5f0a09e1f881" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Cubic Polynomial Given Three Real Roots and a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ea7c6445-1e77-55a1-a103-fbf59b3ce0bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278554}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ea7c6445-1e77-55a1-a103-fbf59b3ce0bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278554} :answer-field/id #uuid "9d31d0b1-e5d7-569a-a5f3-d91ae28a7aab" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278553} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c0297766-a587-54e6-ab3e-f7609ca006f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278556}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c0297766-a587-54e6-ab3e-f7609ca006f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278556} :answer-field/id #uuid "56daa1ba-5fa7-5531-a098-3a49bc93743a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278555} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "50f4fe9b-3ce3-5bdc-8a0f-8fc73e08122b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "140" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278558}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "50f4fe9b-3ce3-5bdc-8a0f-8fc73e08122b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "140" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278558} :answer-field/id #uuid "7d781bba-bc03-5e45-85bd-d3afe7594ae5" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278557}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c70e3f39-8e0c-5cd9-812d-d51cfacc19d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-316630" :question/problem "The cubic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=0,$ ${x}_{2}=-4,$ and ${x}_{3}=7,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $-5.$ Find $P(x).$\n\n$P(x)=$\n{{field-1}}${x}^{3}\\,+$\n{{field-2}}${x}^{2}\\,+$\n{{field-3}}$x$" :question/worked-solution "Since our cubic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}=0,$ ${x}_{2}=-4,$ and ${x}_{3}=7,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=-5,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) & =-5(x-0)(x-(-4))(x-7) \\\\  & =-5\\,x\\,(x+4)(x-7)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5\\,x\\,(x+4)(x-7) & =-5\\,x\\,({x}^{2}-3x-28) \\\\  & =-5({x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}-28x) \\\\  & =-5{x}^{3}+15{x}^{2}+140x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=-5{x}^{3}+15{x}^{2}+140x.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278559 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e4bb90c5-2794-5657-8f0b-45eb64873e03" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Cubic Polynomial Given One Real Root, Two Complex Roots, and a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7408c08e-caee-5dbd-ba6c-af9b034a4b1e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278561} {:answer/id #uuid "34156666-9e7e-54ac-8582-f70fcdf44c58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278562}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7408c08e-caee-5dbd-ba6c-af9b034a4b1e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278561} :answer-field/id #uuid "363f97bb-2fd3-5c2e-a900-6d6e2513e2f2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278560} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ac11729-ece9-584c-aa57-f0fe6eafb376" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278564}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1ac11729-ece9-584c-aa57-f0fe6eafb376" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278564} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b6bf546-57f1-59fd-8e63-c771792fb493" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278563} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cc64eba2-f820-5709-8105-21443673f1c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "66" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278566}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cc64eba2-f820-5709-8105-21443673f1c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "66" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278566} :answer-field/id #uuid "2cf3e197-31d9-5dc9-9311-82b301ee1c0b" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278565} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d0295861-48dc-5412-9bee-d81a1f8c4c21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "90" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278568}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d0295861-48dc-5412-9bee-d81a1f8c4c21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "90" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278568} :answer-field/id #uuid "fa314409-aa55-5e48-b22a-4ca8b499e769" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278567}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "36167bf9-aede-5c11-b082-9cb8c7596265" :question/math-academy-id "q-316652" :question/problem "The cubic polynomial $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=3,{x}_{2,3}=1\\pm 2\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $6.$ Find $f(x).$\n\n$P(x)=$\n{{field-1}}${x}^{3}\\,-$\n{{field-2}}${x}^{2}\\,+$\n{{field-3}}$x\\,-$\n{{field-4}}" :question/worked-solution "Since $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=3$ and ${x}_{2,3}=1\\pm 2\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=6,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =6(x-3)(x-(1+2\\text{i}))(x-(1-2\\text{i}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6(x-3)(x-(1+2\\text{i}))(x-(1-2\\text{i})) & = \\\\ 6(x-3)({x}^{2}-x(1+2\\text{i})-x(1-2\\text{i})+(1+2\\text{i})(1-2\\text{i})) & = \\\\ 6(x-3)({x}^{2}-2x+5) & = \\\\ 6({x}^{3}-5{x}^{2}+11x-15) & = \\\\ 6{x}^{3}-30{x}^{2}+66x-90.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=6{x}^{3}-30{x}^{2}+66x-90.$"}]}
